.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt VIRTIO-GPU 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm virtio-gpu ,
.Nm virtio_gpu ,
.Nm virtio-vga
.Nd DRM driver of the virtio GPU display and virgl 3D
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In drm/drm.h
.In drm/drm_mode.h
.In drm/virtgpu_drm.h
.Pp
.Pa /dev/dri/cardN
.Pa /dev/dri/renderD128+N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver binds the virtio GPU of virtio 1.2, device 16, on the PCI bus:
QEMU's
.Ql -device virtio-gpu-pci ,
a display controller, and
.Ql -device virtio-vga ,
which is a VGA controller as well, as Linux 6.12's virtio_gpu does.
It takes the device's EDID and virgl 3D features when offered.
QEMU's
.Ql -device virtio-vga-gl
offers virgl.
Blob resources and explicit context initialization are not negotiated.
Under virtio-vga the driver first removes the firmware's framebuffer from
every memory BAR of the device, so that
.Xr fbdrm 4
leaves the screen to it and the machine has one card.
.Pp
A bound device is a DRM device, as
.Xr drm 4
describes, registered as
.Ql virtio_gpu
with Linux's identity: description
.Ql virtio GPU ,
version 0.1.0 and date 0, on the PCI bus.
It has a card node and a render node, and the features
.Dv DRIVER_GEM ,
.Dv DRIVER_MODESET ,
.Dv DRIVER_ATOMIC ,
.Dv DRIVER_RENDER ,
.Dv DRIVER_SYNCOBJ ,
.Dv DRIVER_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE
and
.Dv DRIVER_CURSOR_HOTSPOT ;
a device with no scanout has no
.Dv DRIVER_MODESET
or
.Dv DRIVER_ATOMIC ,
and a render node alone serves it.
The kernel logs the device's PCI function as
.Dq virtio_gpu: pci: virtio-vga detected at 0000:BB:DD.F
or
.Dq virtio-gpu-pci ,
the features as Linux's
.Dq features: +virgl +edid -resource_blob -host_visible
and
.Dq features: -context_init ,
the number of scanouts and of capability sets, and each scanout's size
whenever it reads the displays.
.Ss Commands
Every command goes to the device on its control queue, and the cursor's on
the cursor queue.
Each control command carries a fence whose id is the next of the device's
timeline, in the order the commands reach the queue; the device's answer
signals it, and an error answer fails it with
.Er EIO .
When the queue is full, commands wait in order for answers to make room.
A command the driver waits for that has no answer in five seconds fails
with
.Er ETIMEDOUT
and is logged; its late answer is still taken.
Error answers to commands nobody waits for are logged.
.Ss Display
Each scanout has one CRTC with a primary plane of format XRGB8888 and a
cursor plane of ARGB8888, an encoder of type
.Dv DRM_MODE_ENCODER_VIRTUAL
and a connector of type
.Dv DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_VIRTUAL ,
.Ql Virtual-1
and on, connected while the device says its scanout is enabled.
The first scanout counts as enabled at 1024x768 until the device answers.
.Pp
With the EDID feature the connector has the
.Ql EDID
property and its modes are the EDID's: QEMU's lists 26 at its default
1280x800, which is preferred, and its
.Ql xres
and
.Ql yres
choose another.
Without it the modes are the DMT modes up to 8192x8192, with the
scanout's size added as a CVT mode at 60 Hz and preferred, or 1024x768
preferred while the device gives no size.
Framebuffers are 32 to 8192 pixels on a side.
Format modifiers are not supported: planes have no
.Ql IN_FORMATS
property,
.Dv DRM_CAP_ADDFB2_MODIFIERS
is 0, and
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_MODE_ADDFB2
with
.Dv DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS
fails with
.Er EINVAL .
.Pp
A commit that shows a buffer copies the damaged part of a dumb buffer to
the host's resource with
.Dv VIRTIO_GPU_CMD_TRANSFER_TO_HOST_2D ,
sets the scanout again when the buffer, its source rectangle or the mode
changed, and flushes the damaged part to the screen, waiting for the
flush.
The damage is the union of the plane's
.Ql FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS
inside its source, or the whole source when the buffer or the source
changed;
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DIRTYFB
sets the clips.
A plane with no buffer, or a CRTC turned off, leaves the scanout showing
nothing.
The cursor plane sends its buffer's pixels and
.Dv VIRTIO_GPU_CMD_UPDATE_CURSOR
with its hotspot when its buffer changes, and
.Dv VIRTIO_GPU_CMD_MOVE_CURSOR
when it only moves.
.Ss Display changes
When the device reports a display change, such as a resized QEMU window
or a VNC client's
.Ql SetDesktopSize ,
the driver reads the EDIDs and the displays again, clears the event, and
sends the card's
.Dq change
uevent with
.Ql HOTPLUG=1 ,
as Linux does.
The change is served by the kernel thread
.Ql virtio_gpu ,
made at the first open of one of the device's nodes; a change before that
open is served by the open itself, and sends its uevent then.
A program then reads the new modes with
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_MODE_GETCONNECTOR .
.Ss Buffers
Each buffer object is a host resource over pages of system memory, which
are given when the object is made and passed to the device in runs of
adjacent pages; resource ids are the lowest free from 1.
Dumb buffers take 32 bits a pixel alone, have rows of the width's bytes,
unpadded, and a whole number of pages, and their resources are XRGB8888.
Mappings are cached.
When the last reference to a buffer goes, its resource is unreferenced on
the device and its pages are freed once the device answers.
.Ss Ioctls
The render node and the card take Linux's virtio_gpu ioctls:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_MAP
The mmap offset of a buffer.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_GETPARAM
.Dv VIRTGPU_PARAM_CAPSET_QUERY_FIX
is 1.
.Dv VIRTGPU_PARAM_3D_FEATURES
is 1 when virgl was negotiated, and
.Dv VIRTGPU_PARAM_SUPPORTED_CAPSET_IDs
has a bit for each offered capset id.
The other known parameters are 0.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_RESOURCE_CREATE
A resource over a new buffer of the given size, or a page for 0,
returning its handle and resource id.
With virgl it passes the target, format, bind flags, dimensions, array size,
levels, samples and flags to the host.
Without virgl it accepts a 2D resource, target 2, alone.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_RESOURCE_INFO
A buffer's size and resource id.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_TRANSFER_TO_HOST
Copies a box of a buffer to its resource, not waited for; the command's
fence joins the buffer's reservation.
With virgl, the box, level and backing offset go to TRANSFER_TO_HOST_3D.
Nonzero stride and layer stride are refused for these resources.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_WAIT
Waits up to 15 seconds for a buffer's outstanding work, or with
.Dv VIRTGPU_WAIT_NOWAIT
says whether there is any.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_EXECBUFFER
Copies and queues virgl commands and holds the buffers named by the BO
handle list until the host answers.
An input fence descriptor waits for foreign producers; a fence on this
control queue needs no wait, since its commands are ordered already.
An output fence descriptor is a close-on-exec sync file.
Input and output syncobjs, with timeline points, are also accepted.
Submissions queue without waiting for earlier frames to finish.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_TRANSFER_FROM_HOST
Copies a box from the host into the buffer's backing, asynchronously,
with a reservation fence for WAIT.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_GET_CAPS
Reads a supported capability set and version, copying the smaller of the
user's size and the host's size.
A zero size or an unsupported id or version is
.Er EINVAL .
With no capability sets the result is
.Er ENOSYS .
.Pp
EXECBUFFER and TRANSFER_FROM_HOST return
.Er ENOSYS
without virgl.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_RESOURCE_CREATE_BLOB , Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_CONTEXT_INIT
Fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.El
.Ss Device loss
Root may write
.Ql 1
to
.Pa /sys/kernel/debug/dri/N/virtio_gpu_reset
to reset and unplug the virtual GPU.
Every pending fence fails with
.Er ENODEV ,
every context is invalidated, the transport stops DMA and every resource's
backing is freed.
The device nodes disappear, old descriptors' ioctls return
.Er ENODEV
and old mappings fault.
A new boot is needed to use the device again.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/dri/renderD128+N
.It Pa /dev/dri/cardN
The card node of a bound device.
.It Pa /dev/dri/renderD128+N
Its render node.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
Besides those of
.Xr drm 4 :
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBUSY
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_WAIT
while the buffer still has work.
.It Er EINVAL
A dumb buffer of other than 32 bits a pixel; a
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_RESOURCE_CREATE
of a 3D target, depth, array, sample count or more than one level without
virgl; a transfer stride without a blob; ring selection without context
initialization; an
unknown
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_GETPARAM
parameter; a format modifier.
.It Er EIO
The device answered a command with an error.
.It Er ENOENT
No buffer of the handle given.
.It Er ENOSPC
Every resource id is taken.
.It Er ENOSYS
A 3D call without virgl, or GET_CAPS on a device with no capability sets.
.It Er ETIMEDOUT
The device did not answer in five seconds.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr drm 4 ,
.Xr fbdrm 4 ,
.Xr drm-kms 7
.Sh HISTORY
The driver follows Linux 6.12's virtio_gpu.
Its commands are those of virtio 1.2, section 5.7.
.Sh BUGS
Under virtio-vga the screen is QEMU's VGA picture, the firmware's
console, until the driver's first command, and then the device's scanout,
which shows nothing until a program sets a mode, since the console does
not draw on a DRM card.
